{# TM·E — ATTENTION FIRST.

   Everything needing a human decision above everything that does not, which is
   the right shape for an installation somebody opens once a week: you arrive,
   you see what changed, you leave.

   THIS DIRECTION CARRIES ITS OWN ATTENTION PANE, so its preset does not also
   load the separate one — two copies of the same three rows on one page is the
   page saying everything twice.

   In a settled organisation it spends the top of the page saying that nothing
   is wrong, and that is the cost. The settled state is drawn honestly rather
   than hidden: one line, and then the roster. #}
{% import '@UhifadhiTeam/team/_bits.html.twig' as bits %}

<div class="c" data-tm data-tm-dir="e">
    <span class="tab"><span class="idx">TM&middot;E</span>Roster<span class="src">&middot; attention first</span></span>

    {% if overview.needsAttention %}
        <div class="tm-esplit">
            <span class="lbl">Waiting on a decision &mdash; {{ overview.attentionCount }}</span>
            <div class="tm-att">
                {% for person in overview.neverSignedIn %}
                    <div class="tm-attrow w">
                        {{ bits.icon_mail() }}
                        <div class="at">
                            <b>{{ person.fullName }} has never signed in</b>
                            <p>{% if person.wasInvited %}Invited by {{ person.invitedBy ? person.invitedBy.fullName : 'somebody since removed' }}, {{ bits.ago(person.invitedAt) }}.{% else %}Created with a password and never invited, so there is no link outstanding.{% endif %}</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="ad"><a class="softbtn" href="{{ path('team_member', {uuid: person.uuidString}) }}">Open</a></div>
                    </div>
                {% endfor %}
                {% for person in overview.holdNothing %}
                    <div class="tm-attrow w">
                        {{ bits.icon_info() }}
                        <div class="at">
                            <b>{{ person.fullName }} holds nothing</b>
                            <p>Staff with no position: they can sign in and reach no page behind it.</p>
                        </div>
                        <div class="ad"><a class="softbtn acc" href="{{ path('team_member', {uuid: person.uuidString}) }}">Give them a position</a></div>
                    </div>
                {% endfor %}
                {% if overview.soleSuperAdmin %}
                    <div class="tm-attrow r standing">
                        {{ bits.icon_warn() }}
                        <div class="at">
                            <b>{{ overview.soleSuperAdmin.fullName }} is the only Super Admin</b>
                            <p>No second owner and no break-glass. A standing risk rather than a task &mdash; it
                            has no done, so it has no button.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                {% endif %}
            </div>
        </div>
    {% else %}
        <div class="tm-settled">
            {{ bits.icon_check() }}
            <span>Nothing is waiting on a decision: everybody has signed in, everybody holds a position, and
            there is more than one Super Admin. This direction spends its top on that sentence when it is true,
            which is the cost of putting the decisions first.</span>
        </div>
    {% endif %}

    <span class="lbl" style="margin-top:16px;display:block">The settled roster</span>
    <div class="tm-scroll">
        <table class="tbl">
            <thead><tr><th>Person</th><th>Tier</th><th>Position</th><th>Account</th><th></th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                {% for person in everybody %}
                    <tr class="{{ person.isActive ? '' : 'tm-off' }}">
                        <td>{{ bits.person(person, person == app.user) }}</td>
                        <td>{{ bits.tier_pill(person.teamRole) }}</td>
                        <td>{{ bits.position_cell(person, path('team_positions')) }}</td>
                        <td>{{ bits.account_cell(person) }}</td>
                        <td class="tm-acts">{{ bits.open_button(person) }}</td>
                    </tr>
                {% endfor %}
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </div>
</div>
